Package: RAssistant
Title: A Lightweight AI Assistant for RStudio
Version: 0.15.0
Authors@R: person("MySimpleSmart", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "120612480+MySimpleSmart@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Opens the existing Source-aware chat assistant in the RStudio
    Viewer. Supports image uploads, optional live console context, contextual R help,
    a project Knowledge Base (PDFs, notes, R examples and custom instructions),
    reviewed Source edits and explicitly approved script validation. Stores optional credentials
    in the operating system credential store, separately from package updates.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports:
    askpass,
    callr,
    commonmark,
    ellmer (>= 0.5.0),
    htmltools,
    httpuv,
    jsonlite,
    keyring (>= 1.3.0),
    knitr,
    later,
    remotes,
    rlang,
    rstudioapi,
    shiny (>= 1.14.0)
Suggests:
    httr2,
    pdftools
URL: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant
BugReports: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant/issues
Config/RAssistant/Changes: Choose OpenAI, Claude, Gemini, DeepSeek, Groq, Mistral, OpenRouter, Perplexity, Hugging Face, xAI, Together AI, Fireworks AI or Cerebras in API settings. Add other services through an HTTPS OpenAI-compatible endpoint and an exact model ID.
    Keep separate provider keys in the OS credential store and remember non-secret model settings locally. Switch providers without reopening the chat; existing OpenAI keys keep working. First launch can configure any provider without an OpenAI key.
    Keep credentials out of update checks, validation subprocesses and captured Console context. Keep failed messages and their attachments ready to retry after authentication or model errors.
